D. Abstract Data Types (ADT)
11. Predict the Output – Stack ADT Concept
#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;
#define SIZE 5
int stack[SIZE];
int top = -1;
void push(int x) {
stack[++top] = x;
}
int pop() {
return stack[top--];
}
int main() {
push(10);
push(20);
push(30);
printf(&quot;%d &quot;, pop());
printf(&quot;%d &quot;, pop());
return 0;
}
Question: Predict the output and identify the ADT operation being performed.
Stack ADT
Operations:
push(10);
push(20);
push(30);
Stack becomes:
30  ← top
20
10
Stack follows LIFO — Last In, First Out.
First:
pop()
removes 30.
Second:
pop()
removes 20.
Output:
30 20
ADT operation: pop() — removes and returns the top element.
